# Wave 4b. Where the policy lives.

file: "packages/editor/src/shell/app.tsx"
doc: "Root shell: adapters, document state, stores, and reconciling external file changes."

constants: [
  { name: "App"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Additions only; load/open, the two stores, the theme wiring and the\n"
      "Resizable layout are unchanged.\n"
      "\n"
      "On load, keep the LoadResult's baseHash and stamp, and hand the hash to\n"
      "createSaveController.\n"
      "\n"
      "Start watchOnFocus for the session. When it reports a change, the\n"
      "response depends on whether the user has unsaved work:\n"
      "\n"
      "  clean (state.dirty() is false) — adopt the incoming stylesheet\n"
      "    directly and adopt its hash. There is nothing to conflict with, and\n"
      "    making someone review changes they have no stake in is noise. This\n"
      "    is what every editor does with a clean buffer.\n"
      "\n"
      "  dirty — append change.edit to the CURRENT stylesheet's pendingEdits\n"
      "    rather than replacing anything. ghost_layer already draws pending\n"
      "    edits as a dimmed overlay, so the external change arrives as\n"
      "    something to look at while the user's own work stays exactly where\n"
      "    it was. Do NOT adopt the hash here: the document on disk still\n"
      "    differs from what is in memory, so saving must stay refused until\n"
      "    the edit is accepted or rejected.\n"
      "\n"
      "A change whose `edit` is undefined means the file was rewritten with\n"
      "identical content — adopt the new stamp and hash, show nothing.\n"
      "\n"
      "Show a banner while a save is stale, saying the file changed and that\n"
      "the change is waiting in the pending list. Wave 7's panel replaces it."
    type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "Component<{}>" } }
    uses: ["watchOnFocus", "createSaveController", "createScene", "createUiState", "getBundledTheme", "applyEditorTheme"]
  }
]
